; SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
; The owner's session at CART.9's third hand test, 2026-10-21, and a stand-in after it (decisions 14 and 26), so that
; the page's hand, the block hand-naught, holds a replay of the game and of the bench. Frames 1 to 45 are the owner's,
; as the owner's page recorded them: the load's act on the Lesson; on I NON the switch toggled by Space twice, set by
; 1 and 0, clicked twice, NON written from NON-ET and passed, and N; on II ET, VEL written where ET is due and the test
; stopping at input 2, then ET by NON of NON-ET, passed at its least known. Since CART.9's short slice of 2026-10-24
; those rows play against the cartridge as it stands, each act in the frames it took. Then a stand-in written by the
; engine's own steps in the form the host's recorder writes, each act's Input rows those that differ from the ones last
; logged, the engine releasing a press and a command after each: the levels III to IX of the engine's scripted
; session, III's input emptied by Delete, its error named before T and where the test stops, R, and a pass; IV's AUT
; with a gate outside the set, VEL times a number written as a text, which is no gate, one star; V at its least known;
; VI at the textbook's three gates, two stars; VII with two gates idle and outside the set, one star, which their
; Delete moves not until T again, three; VIII at its least known; and IX's four whole sums, a carry rippling, its 512
; inputs in 514 frames. Then the bench's 38 switches, each written in the drawer's edit row, its tab chosen at the
; first: the adder's a to all ones and its carry-in, 65,535 + 1 rippling through all sixteen bits; the multiplier's
; 255 x 255 = 65,025; and the low bits turned back, 254 x 127 = 32,258. And last, I's switch written over, which the
; test no longer drives, so that it stops at input 1. Every frame of the bench and of the game is held to the hand:
; the gates, the boards, the words, the Lab, the Gates sheet and the Camera's sheet. Its golden is the Bench's record
; at its end.
